{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"On an unconfined macOS run, a killed grandchild can remain an unreaped zombie long enough for the cleanup assertion to fail even though cleanup succeeded."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"test","trigger":"unusual","reason":"If Linux process information is unavailable, the test helper can accept a still-running process as stopped and miss a cleanup failure."}]}